### Describe the feature you'd like to request

I would love the ability to globally handle errors that happen when making server side calls with `createCaller()` to avoid repeating the same error handling code in many different places.

### Describe the solution you'd like to see

For example, Next.js exposes a [`notFound()`](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/functions/not-found) function that throws `NEXT_NOT_FOUND` error and terminates rendering of the route segment in which it was thrown. I would like to catch every tRPC's `NOT_FOUND` error and call Next.js' `notFound()` instead. It would be great if I could define that custom error handling logic once, when creating a caller or caller factory.

```ts
import { notFound } from "next/navigation";

// t = initTRPC.create({ ... });

const createCaller = t.createCallerFactory(router);

const caller = createCaller(createServerContext, {
  onError: ({ ctx, error, input, path, req, type }) => {
    if (error.code === "NOT_FOUND") notFound();
    throw error; // rethrow other errors to be handled at the procedure call level
  },
});
```

### Describe alternate solutions

I have considered:

- Calling `notFound()` inside of the procedures (tRPC catches the error)
- Using middleware (tRPC catches the error)
- Using [create-t3-app's implementation of the RSC client](https://github.com/t3-oss/create-t3-app/blob/main/cli/template/extras/src/trpc/server.ts) and a custom link instead of the `t.createCallerFactory()` (tRPC catches the error but it could have been due to my lack of understanding how links work)
- Creating a wrapper function that takes a procedure path as an argument, calls the procedure, catches the error and implements error handling logic (requires some more advanced knowledge of TypeScript to preserve type-safety and changes the API to something similar to `callerWrapper((caller) => caller.subrouter.procedure())`)
- Using JavaScript [`Proxy`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Proxy) to intercept every method call and handle the errors (I think it's possible to do but I wasn't able to make it work)
- Defining `handleNotFound()` function and appending `.catch(handleNotFound)` to every procedure call that requires it (this is what I'm using at the moment, but requires code repetition).

### Additional information

Similar discussion but this one is about global error handling on the client side (https://github.com/trpc/trpc/discussions/2036).

### 👨‍👧‍👦 Contributing

- [X] 🙋‍♂️ Yes, I'd be down to file a PR implementing this feature!
